From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pradeep P V K <pradeep.pragallapati@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:54:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom-qmp-ufs: Add Glymur support

Add the init sequence tables and config for the UFS QMP phy found in
the Glymur SoC.

Similar to SM8750, the QSERDES RX and TX register offsets for
glymur SoC follow the v7 register layout, while the remaining
(PCS, MPHY base) register offsets follow v6 layout. Update the
register layouts accordingly.

Reviewed-by: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@oss.qualcomm.com>
Acked-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Manivannan Sadhasivam <manivannan.sadhasivam@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Pradeep P V K <pradeep.pragallapati@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261028-glymur_ufs_qcb_enablement-v5-3-09cda5e3bab3@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Vinod Koul <vkoul@kernel.org>
[birk: second hunk on 7.3's context, where the regulator tables follow
qphy_clrbits() and not struct qmp_ufs. The added lines are unchanged.]
